media: qcom: camss: add SM6375

SM6375 (and SM4375 "blair") has three TFE530/CSID530 pairs, laid out as
qcm2290's (VFE and CSID 340: the CSID at the start of each TFE block,
the TFE core 0x1000 above it), and four CSIPHYs of the 1.2.1 generation
(sm8250's lane table; the downstream driver writes 0x80 instead of 0x60
to each lane's 0x14). Clock rates follow GCC's tables and the downstream
DT. There is no interconnect driver for SM6375 yet: no paths.

CSID 340's PHY select field is three bits wide (downstream csid530:
csi2_rx_phy_num_mask 0x7); with two bits, CSIPHY3 (value 4) selected none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

